---
const {kind} = Astro.props;
---
{kind === 'chain' && <figure class="pgb-figure pgb-chain" data-pgb-chain aria-labelledby="pgb-chain-title">
  <figcaption id="pgb-chain-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Two stretches of WAL, two different checks</figcaption>
  <div class="pgb-panel">
    <label class="pgb-option">Later archive <select data-archive aria-label="Later archive for figure 1"><option value="complete">Complete</option><option value="gap">Required segment missing</option></select></label>
    <div class="pgb-copy"><strong>Base backup</strong><span>Files copied while the source runs</span><span class="pgb-small">backup_label · tablespace map · manifest</span></div>
    <div class="pgb-arrow">↓ replay the backup’s consistency WAL</div>
    <div class="pgb-consistency"><strong>WAL bundled by <code>--wal-method=stream</code></strong><span>Makes this backup consistent at its end</span><span class="pgb-tag">Checked by pg_verifybackup</span></div>
    <div class="pgb-arrow">↓ later archived WAL continues the same history</div>
    <ol class="pgb-segments" aria-label="Illustrative later WAL dependency order">
      <li><strong>Earlier segment</strong><span>After backup completion</span><b>Available</b></li>
      <li data-segment><strong>Required segment</strong><span>WAL leading to the target</span><b data-live data-gap-label>Available</b></li>
      <li data-beyond><strong>Target segment</strong><span>Contains before_price_mistake</span><b data-live data-beyond-label>Reachable</b></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="pgb-message" data-live data-chain-result aria-live="polite">Both checks are needed: the base verifies, and replay can reach the named target through the later archive.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="pgb-caption">A dependency drawing, without real filenames or LSNs. Segments are placed to show the distinction. Removing later WAL does not change the intact base backup or its manifest result.</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><p>A streamed base backup includes the WAL needed for its own consistency. A later target also needs every intervening archived segment in the selected history. If a required later segment is missing, a valid base and later files cannot bridge that gap.</p></details>
</figure>}
{kind === 'branch' && <figure class="pgb-figure" aria-labelledby="pgb-branch-title">
  <figcaption id="pgb-branch-title"><span>Figure 2</span> Finishing recovery creates another history</figcaption>
  <div class="pgb-panel pgb-branch">
    <div class="pgb-origin"><strong>Shared history</strong><span>Order 103 · pending · 29.00</span><span>Stock 10 / 0 / 4 · P7 20.00</span></div>
    <div class="pgb-cut"><strong>before_price_mistake</strong><span>Named WAL record after backup completion</span></div>
    <div class="pgb-fork"><div class="pgb-old"><strong>Original timeline →</strong><span>Mistake: P7 → 2.20</span><span>Then payment 504 → 10.00</span><b>Preserve evidence; close source writes</b></div><div class="pgb-new"><strong>New timeline →</strong><span>Finish the verified earlier recovery</span><span>Reconcile payment 504 → 10.00</span><b>P7 20.00 · 19.00 still due</b></div></div>
    <div class="pgb-provider"><strong>Provider history · outside PostgreSQL</strong><span>Accepted 10.00 · order-103-part-payment-1</span><span>The database restore does not rewind it</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="pgb-caption">A model of this recovery branch, not elapsed time. The timeline history file records where the new branch left its parent. Both branches retain the agreed order total; only the original branch contains the price mistake.</p>
</figure>}
{kind === 'restore' && <figure class="pgb-figure pgb-restore" data-pgb-restore aria-labelledby="pgb-restore-title">
  <figcaption id="pgb-restore-title"><span>Figure 3</span> A paused target is an inspection point</figcaption>
  <div class="pgb-panel">
    <label class="pgb-option">Provider evidence <select data-provider aria-label="Provider evidence for figure 3"><option value="accepted">Known accepted, exact match</option><option value="unknown">Outcome unresolved</option></select></label>
    <div class="pgb-state-grid"><div><strong>Original source</strong><b data-live data-source>Separate, still preserved</b><span data-live data-source-detail>Its later work is outside this restore</span></div><div class="pgb-target"><strong>Restored candidate</strong><b data-live data-target>Copied base · not started</b><code data-live data-native>recovery.signal</code></div></div>
    <dl class="pgb-facts"><div><dt>P7 price</dt><dd data-live data-price>Not inspected</dd></div><div><dt>Order 103</dt><dd data-live data-order>Not inspected</dd></div><div><dt>Payment 504</dt><dd data-live data-payment>Not inspected</dd></div><div><dt>Recorded due</dt><dd data-live data-due>Not inspected</dd></div></dl>
    <p class="pgb-gate" data-live data-gate>Ordinary callers and external dispatch excluded</p>
    <p class="pgb-message" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">Copy the verified base into a separate target. Keep the original backup and archive unchanged.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pgb-controls" role="group" aria-label="Playback for figure 3"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 6</span><div class="pgb-hold" data-hold><span></span></div></div>
  <p class="pgb-caption">A controlled recovery schedule. Source closure includes in-flight database and provider outcomes. The accepted option assumes a hypothetical retained, queryable provider result; no real provider is contacted.</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><ol><li>Copy the verified backup and configure an isolated target.</li><li>Replay the chosen source history to the named point and verify that recovery has actually paused.</li><li>Read the recovered facts: P7 20.00; pending order 103, total 29.00; no payment 504; stock 10/0/4.</li><li>Close source writes and dispatch, account for in-flight outcomes and retain final evidence.</li><li>Finish the verified recovery under controlled access. A matching known accepted provider result supports recording payment 504 and its original identity once. An unresolved result does not.</li><li>Verify the final balance and one write authority before restoring the relevant service. Keep unresolved payment work restricted.</li></ol></details>
</figure>}
<script>
import {stepper} from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-pgb-chain]')) {
 const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-archive]')!;
 const draw=()=>{
  const gap=select.value==='gap';
  root.querySelector('[data-segment]')!.classList.toggle('pgb-missing',gap);
  root.querySelector('[data-beyond]')!.classList.toggle('pgb-unreachable',gap);
  root.querySelector('[data-gap-label]')!.textContent=gap?'Missing':'Available';
  root.querySelector('[data-beyond-label]')!.textContent=gap?'Unreachable':'Reachable';
  root.querySelector('[data-chain-result]')!.textContent=gap?'The base still verifies. Replay stops before the missing segment; files beyond it cannot make the target reachable.':'Both checks are needed: the base verifies, and replay can reach the named target through the later archive.';
 }; select.addEventListener('change',draw); draw();
}
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-pgb-restore]')) {
 const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-provider]')!;
 const set=(name:string,value:string)=>root.querySelector(`[data-${name}]`)!.textContent=value;
 const text=[
 'Copy the verified base into a separate target. Keep the original backup and archive unchanged.',
 'Recovery reads the required WAL, reaches before_price_mistake and pauses. Confirm the actual paused state and the target message in the server log.',
 'Inspect the paused database. P7 is 20.00; order 103 is pending for 29.00; payment 504 is absent. The purchase and its stock changes were retained.',
 'Close original source writes and external dispatch. Account for operations already in flight, preserve final outcomes and prevent old clients from writing again.',
 'Finish this verified recovery under controlled access. Reconcile only the known accepted 10.00 charge, with its original identity and payment 504, in one database transaction.',
 'Verify one payment, 19.00 due and unchanged stock. The old source stays fenced. Resume callers and dispatch only after their outstanding work is accounted for.'
 ];
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>6,draw:(step:number)=>{
  const accepted=select.value==='accepted';
  set('source',step<3?'Separate, still preserved':'Closed to authoritative writes');
  set('source-detail',step<3?'Its later work is outside this restore':'Final outcomes retained · old authority fenced');
  set('target',step===0?'Copied base · not started':step<4?'In recovery · paused at target':'Recovery complete · controlled access');
  set('native',step===0?'recovery.signal':step<4?"pg_get_wal_replay_pause_state() = paused":'pg_is_in_recovery() = false');
  set('price',step<2?'Not inspected':'20.00');
  set('order',step<2?'Not inspected':'Pending · 29.00');
  set('payment',step<2?'Not inspected':step>=4&&accepted?'One · 10.00':'Absent');
  set('due',step<2?'Not inspected':step>=4&&accepted?'19.00':'29.00');
  set('gate',step===5&&accepted?'Ready only after service and dispatch checks':step>=4&&!accepted?'Payment unresolved · relevant work remains restricted':'Ordinary callers and external dispatch excluded');
  root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=step>=4&&!accepted?(step===4?'Recovery can finish under controlled access, but the provider outcome remains unresolved. Do not infer “no charge” from the restored absence or issue another charge.':'The restored database is usable for inspection, but this payment is still an open exception. Keep its work restricted until the original outcome can be established.'):text[step];
 }}); select.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
}
</script>
<style>
.pgb-figure{--pgb-line:color-mix(in srgb,var(--color-text) 55%,var(--color-surface-alt));margin:2.5rem 0; font:.84rem/1.55 var(--font-sans); color:var(--color-text);}
figcaption{font:1.2rem/1.35 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:.7rem;}
figcaption>span{font:.65rem var(--font-mono);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.6rem;white-space:nowrap;}
.pgb-panel{border:1px solid var(--pgb-line);background:var(--color-surface-alt);padding:1.2rem;}
.pgb-figure strong,.pgb-figure b,.pgb-figure span{display:block;}
.pgb-option{display:flex;gap:.75rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:1.2rem;font-size:.8rem;}
select,button{font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border:1px solid var(--pgb-line);border-radius:4px;padding:.45rem .6rem;}
button{cursor:pointer;}
select:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:3px;}
.pgb-copy,.pgb-consistency,.pgb-origin,.pgb-cut{border:1px solid var(--pgb-line);padding:.8rem 1rem;}
.pgb-copy{border-left:3px solid var(--purple);}
.pgb-consistency{border-left:3px solid var(--teal);}
.pgb-small,.pgb-caption{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);}
.pgb-tag{font-size:.75rem;color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 75%,var(--color-text));margin-top:.4rem;}
.pgb-arrow{font:.75rem/1.5 var(--font-mono);padding:.7rem 1rem;}
.pgb-segments{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.7rem;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:.2rem 0 1rem;}
.pgb-segments li{border:1px solid var(--teal);padding:.8rem;position:relative;overflow-wrap:anywhere;}
.pgb-segments li:not(:last-child):after{content:'→';position:absolute;right:-.65rem;top:45%;background:var(--color-surface-alt);z-index:1;}
.pgb-segments b{color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 75%,var(--color-text));font-size:.75rem;margin-top:.6rem;}
.pgb-segments .pgb-missing{border:2px dashed var(--coral);}
.pgb-segments .pgb-missing b{color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--coral) 75%,var(--color-text));}
.pgb-segments .pgb-unreachable{border-color:var(--pgb-line);border-style:dashed;}
.pgb-segments .pgb-unreachable b{color:var(--color-text-secondary);}
.pgb-message{border-left:3px solid var(--teal);padding:.5rem 0 .5rem .8rem;min-height:4rem;margin:.8rem 0 0;}
.pgb-caption{margin:.65rem 0;line-height:1.6;}
.pgb-figure details{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);}
.pgb-figure summary{cursor:pointer;padding:.35rem 0;}
.pgb-cut{margin-top:.8rem;border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 75%,var(--color-text));}
.pgb-fork{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;margin:0 0 1rem;padding:0 1rem;}
.pgb-fork>div{border-left:2px solid var(--pgb-line);padding:1rem .8rem .5rem;}
.pgb-fork .pgb-new{border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 75%,var(--color-text));}
.pgb-fork b{font-size:.75rem;margin-top:.6rem;}
.pgb-old b{color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--coral) 75%,var(--color-text));}.pgb-new b{color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 75%,var(--color-text));}
.pgb-provider{border:1px dashed var(--purple);padding:.8rem 1rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere;}
.pgb-state-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;}
.pgb-state-grid>div{padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--pgb-line);}
.pgb-state-grid b{font-weight:500;margin:.4rem 0;}.pgb-state-grid span,.pgb-state-grid code{font-size:.75rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere;}
.pgb-facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.8rem;padding:1rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--pgb-line);margin:0;}
.pgb-facts dt{font-size:.72rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);}.pgb-facts dd{margin:.2rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;}
.pgb-gate{font-size:.75rem;color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--coral) 75%,var(--color-text));}
.pgb-controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--pgb-line);border-top:0;background:var(--color-surface-alt);}
.pgb-controls>span{font:.72rem var(--font-mono);margin-left:auto;}
button[aria-disabled=true]{color:var(--color-text-secondary);cursor:default;}
.pgb-hold{height:2px;flex-basis:100%;background:var(--color-rule);}.pgb-hold span{height:100%;width:0;background:var(--teal);}
@media(max-width:550px){.pgb-panel{padding:.9rem;}.pgb-segments,.pgb-fork,.pgb-state-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.pgb-segments li:not(:last-child):after{content:'↓';right:50%;top:auto;bottom:-.85rem;}.pgb-segments{gap:1rem;}.pgb-facts{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;}.pgb-fork{gap:0;}.pgb-message{min-height:7rem;}figcaption{font-size:1.1rem;}.pgb-option select{max-width:100%;}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.pgb-hold span{transition:none!important;}}
</style>
